1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,627
This is not a tour of a demo.

2
00:00:01,627 --> 00:00:14,858
It is a new tour, built from nothing in CUE: a blank workspace, a real venue list, imported files, a design decision, an agent that finds the problem, and a tour that ends checked, priced, signed and ready.

3
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:21,178
We start with six fields: artist, title, tour, the first room and the date.

4
00:00:21,178 --> 00:00:22,864
No sample data underneath.

5
00:00:22,864 --> 00:00:27,735
Harbour Lights, The Long Way Round, Kade 12 in Amsterdam, in November.

6
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:34,545
Create my tour gives a valid workspace — one venue, one look, one cue, no budget.

7
00:00:34,545 --> 00:00:39,404
The checklist is the path: venue, look, cue sheet, budget, date.

8
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:41,512
Now make it the real tour.

9
00:00:41,512 --> 00:00:42,349
The team.

10
00:00:42,349 --> 00:00:49,625
A second room, The Foundry in Manchester: a twelve by eight stage, twenty-three kilowatts, a four-hundred-kilo rig rating.

11
00:00:49,625 --> 00:00:50,639
A second date.

12
00:00:50,639 --> 00:00:53,776
Two rooms with different limits — that is what a tour is.

13
00:00:54,480 --> 00:01:00,338
Instead of typing the rig, import the Vectorworks fixture schedule: twenty fixtures, twelve beams.

14
00:01:00,338 --> 00:01:03,687
Import the grandMA3 cue list: twelve cues.

15
00:01:03,687 --> 00:01:06,906
The files are parsed in the browser; nothing is uploaded.

16
00:01:06,906 --> 00:01:11,434
The blank placeholder cue is removed, so the sheet is the console's list.

17
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:17,007
Build the look on the imported rig: all twenty fixtures, lime and cyan.

18
00:01:17,007 --> 00:01:22,644
The app computes twenty-seven point three kilowatts and four hundred and forty kilos on the front truss.

19
00:01:22,644 --> 00:01:24,672
This is the show the designer wants.

20
00:01:25,390 --> 00:01:28,040
Now the app does the work a production office does.

21
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:29,420
Kade 12 can take it.

22
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:37,840
The Foundry has twenty-three kilowatts and a four-hundred-kilo rating: the checks name the room, the limit and the gap — before anyone plugs anything in.

23
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:39,527
Ask the agent.

24
00:01:39,527 --> 00:01:47,051
It reads this tour, calls the read-only tools and answers with the numbers: The Foundry, and a reduced look as the cheaper option.

25
00:01:47,051 --> 00:01:48,808
The tool trace is on the right.

26
00:01:48,808 --> 00:01:50,848
It proposes; it does not apply.

27
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:58,669
So the designer makes the decision: a seven-beam cut, nineteen point one kilowatts and three hundred and twenty-six kilos.

28
00:01:58,669 --> 00:01:59,507
Select it.

29
00:01:59,507 --> 00:02:01,417
The checks pass in both rooms.

30
00:02:01,417 --> 00:02:07,313
This is the loop the product is for — propose, check, decide, and the numbers follow the decision.

31
00:02:08,010 --> 00:02:09,952
The money is not a separate spreadsheet.

32
00:02:09,952 --> 00:02:14,728
Add the real lines: rig and crew, five crew for two days, the van.

33
00:02:14,728 --> 00:02:18,172
The true total is twelve thousand seven hundred and forty-four.

34
00:02:18,172 --> 00:02:22,122
The first approval was twelve thousand — seven hundred and forty-four over.

35
00:02:22,122 --> 00:02:27,004
The producer approves thirteen thousand; the tour is two hundred and fifty-six under.

36
00:02:27,004 --> 00:02:29,245
Every look re-prices against that number.

37
00:02:29,950 --> 00:02:31,374
Sign the safety cues.

38
00:02:31,374 --> 00:02:34,251
The sheet the crew gets is the sheet the checks were reading.

39
00:02:34,251 --> 00:02:37,588
Export CSV, HTML or JSON.

40
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:42,672
From six empty fields to a tour that is checked, priced, signed and ready.

41
00:02:42,672 --> 00:02:49,240
The band and the rooms are invented; the arithmetic, the imports, the agent and the decisions are real.

42
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:51,834
CUE designs; the crew runs the show.
